# Panel 105, the spec-warden's find: a type parameter that appears NOWHERE in
# the signature — not in a parameter, not in the result — compiled at exit 0
# until 2026-09-03. No argument can bind it and no context reaches it, so every
# call would be refused; the declaration is the one line that can be fixed, and
# it is refused there, once (Swift's rule: "Generic parameter 'T' is not used
# in function signature").
function unused<A>(what: str) -> str  #~ cannot_infer
    return what

function main()
    print(unused(what: "a"))
